1
00:00:02,120 --> 00:00:02,950
Hey, guys!

2
00:00:03,033 --> 00:00:04,420
This is Miss Asuna.

3
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:08,300
Miss Asuna, this is my
guild, the Sleeping Knights!

4
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:12,040
My name's June. What's up? How's it going?

5
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:16,037
Hi, Miss Asuna.

6
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:16,977
I'm talking.

7
00:00:17,060 --> 00:00:18,560
It's nice to meet you.

8
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:21,877
You really need to get a
grip on those nerves, Tal.

9
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:22,790
Seriously.

10
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:26,297
Every time you meet a girl, you
turn into a blubbering mess.

11
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:29,197
Anyway, my name's Nori. Glad to meet ya.

12
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:30,700
My name is Siyune.

13
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:32,457
It's wonderful to meet you.

14
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:34,817
And thank you so much for coming today.

15
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:36,357
It's a pleasure to meet you.

16
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:37,381
My name's Techi.

17
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:38,830
And?

18
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,324
I'm Yuki, the leader of
this guild, kinda sorta.

19
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:44,860
Miss Asuna, don't laugh.

20
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:49,119
But see, we want to be the only
guild to beat the boss on this floor.

21
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:51,440
And we want you to help us! Huh?

22
00:00:54,060 --> 00:00:54,890
Huh?

23
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:17,460
Thank you.

24
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:41,640
Thank you.

25
00:02:31,180 --> 00:02:35,880
That's very ambitious, but a boss raid
usually takes at least 49 players.

26
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:38,677
That's seven parties with
seven players apiece.

27
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:42,817
So no matter how skilled you are with
just seven players, that's kind of...

28
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:45,537
Well, to be perfectly
honest, it's unrealistic.

29
00:02:45,620 --> 00:02:47,385
Yeah, it sort of is, isn't it?

30
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:51,820
We tried taking on the bosses
on Floor 25 and 6 the same way.

31
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:53,710
Huh?

32
00:02:53,793 --> 00:02:54,623
Just you six?

33
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:55,910
Yep.

34
00:02:55,993 --> 00:02:58,317
And if you ask me, we put
up a pretty good fight, too.

35
00:02:58,400 --> 00:02:59,900
But both times,

36
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:04,877
this huge guilt swooped in and beat him
before we could figure out our next move.

37
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:06,660
Why would you even risk it?

38
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:09,030
That's a story.

39
00:03:09,113 --> 00:03:11,937
It goes back to when we met
in another GamesNet community.

40
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:15,549
We hit it off right away, and
we've been friends ever since.

41
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:19,909
But we only have until next
spring to go on quests together.

42
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:23,571
Since our time's limited, we
wanted to make the most of it.

43
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,660
You see, come spring, we'll
all be busy with other things.

44
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:31,077
So we decided that before
we disbanded the guild,

45
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:35,689
we had to do something so amazing, so
unbelievable, we'd remember it forever.

46
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:39,420
So that's why you want to
do this boss raid. Exactly.

47
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:41,437
If we defeat a boss together,

48
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:44,317
our names will be inscribed
on the Monument of Swordsmen.

49
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:48,518
You know, the one in the Town of
Beginnings, in the Black Iron Palace.

50
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:52,180
I know it sounds silly, and
maybe even a little vain,

51
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:56,480
but we really want to get our names
up on that wall, no matter what.

52
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:59,791
But getting them on there's the hard part.

53
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:02,440
If a boss is defeated by a party,

54
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:05,797
then all of its members will get
their names inscribed on the monument.

55
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:09,077
But if it's beaten by multiple
parties working in tandem,

56
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:12,101
only the names of the party
leaders get inscribed.

57
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:14,360
That's the catch.

58
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:17,817
If we want the names of everyone in
the sleeping nights up on that wall,

59
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:19,480
we have to beat the boss.

60
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:21,900
Together, just us, no one else.

61
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:25,067
So we talked it over
and came up with a plan.

62
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:29,060
A party can have up to seven
players max. Therefore,

63
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:33,937
we decided to find someone as strong or
even stronger than our most powerful player,

64
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:34,850
Yuki,

65
00:04:34,933 --> 00:04:37,960
and hope whoever we found
accepted our invitation.

66
00:04:38,660 --> 00:04:39,740
I get it.

67
00:04:39,940 --> 00:04:41,587
That's why you were dueling.

68
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:44,960
Well, what do you think
about joining up with us?

69
00:04:45,140 --> 00:04:48,846
We can't pay you very much, but
you're welcome to what we have.

70
00:04:49,620 --> 00:04:50,940
Oh no, that's okay.

71
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:54,757
Boss rates cost a fortune as it is,
so you should use your money for that.

72
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:57,428
I'd feel horrible taking
your money, really.

73
00:04:57,600 --> 00:05:01,077
If you want, you could give me whatever
the boss drops and I'll be fine.

74
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:01,990
Really?

75
00:05:02,073 --> 00:05:03,488
Then you'll join our party?

76
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:23,337
This is nothing like
how the old Aincrad was.

77
00:05:23,420 --> 00:05:29,420
And yet, here I am thinking about
safety margins and the odds of winning.

78
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:34,200
Having safe fights and certain victories.

79
00:05:34,820 --> 00:05:36,960
There's more fun to games than that!

80
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:43,040
I bet Yuki and her
friends already know this.

81
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:45,260
Better than I do.

82
00:05:50,180 --> 00:05:52,557
Okay, let's see how far we can go. Yes!

83
00:05:52,640 --> 00:05:55,897
In the end, it's not about winning
or losing, it's having fun.

84
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:57,568
Thanks a bunch, Miss Asuna!

85
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:02,141
Please, I'd prefer it if
you just called me Asuna.

86
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:04,340
Then you can call me Yuki.

87
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:09,280
That reminds me, Miss Yuki, sorry, Yuki,

88
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:12,077
the duel was all about
testing players, right?

89
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:13,160
Yep, pretty much.

90
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:18,077
Then you must have gone up against a ton
of strong players before I showed up.

91
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:20,777
Do you remember ever fighting
a spriggan dressed in black?

92
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:26,057
he would have been using a
one-handed sword huh you know

93
00:06:26,140 --> 00:06:32,057
what I do man he was pretty tough
then why didn't you ask him to

94
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:38,157
help you out I don't know he
just wasn't right well why not

95
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:41,677
he found out my secret I can't

96
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:48,100
have that okay so for tomorrow.

97
00:06:48,420 --> 00:06:49,977
How about we meet back here at 1?

98
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:51,160
You got it!

99
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:54,020
And let's have fun. Great!

100
00:07:37,940 --> 00:07:39,820
Mom, what are you doing?

101
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:47,677
Last month, when you were late for dinner,
I told you it better not happen again.

102
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:48,701
And here we are.

103
00:07:48,860 --> 00:07:52,617
You're late because of that game,
so now you lose your privileges.

104
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:54,340
I just lost track of time.

105
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:56,377
That's my fault, and I'm sorry.

106
00:07:56,460 --> 00:07:59,037
But you didn't have to go and
pull the plug on me like that.

107
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:01,557
You could have shaken me
or even yelled in my ear.

108
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:04,117
I would have gotten an alert in-game,
and then I could have logged out and…

109
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:05,717
I tried that approach before.

110
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:08,918
It took you five minutes to
snap out of it, remember?

111
00:08:09,140 --> 00:08:09,970
Well, yeah.

112
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:12,957
I had to say goodbye to
everyone before I logged in.

113
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:13,870
Oh, don't give me that.

114
00:08:13,953 --> 00:08:16,777
What you do in some stupid
virtual game does not

115
00:08:16,860 --> 00:08:20,400
take priority over your commitments
in the real world. Ever.

116
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:24,780
I'm sorry.

117
00:08:26,340 --> 00:08:28,320
I'll be more careful next time.

118
00:08:29,940 --> 00:08:31,764
This will be your last warning.

119
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:36,908
If you break your word to me because of
that thing again, I'm confiscating it.

120
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:40,118
I have no idea what's going
on in that head of yours.

121
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:43,017
You lost two years of
your life because of that…

122
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:45,629
That infernal machine,
you could have died.

123
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:48,580
How can you even stand to look at it?

124
00:08:50,220 --> 00:08:52,620
This isn't the nerve gear, Mother.

125
00:08:58,220 --> 00:08:59,480
It's dinner time.

126
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:01,842
Get changed and come downstairs.

127
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:04,680
I'm not hungry.

128
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:06,580
As you wish.

129
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:24,830
I don't know.

130
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:12,280
ORGAN PLAYS

131
00:10:22,780 --> 00:10:25,160
Sounds like a good lineup, right?

132
00:10:28,140 --> 00:10:28,970
Asuna!

133
00:10:31,040 --> 00:10:32,340
So, Yuki, Jun,

134
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:36,460
and Tachi are up front, then
Tolkien and Nori are mid-range,

135
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:39,080
and Siyune are the backup? Right.

136
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:43,597
Then I guess, if you're covered, maybe
I should hang back as the rear guard.

137
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:44,880
Yeah, sorry.

138
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:47,997
I feel bad you're not up front
when you're so good with a sword.

139
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:49,492
Oh, I don't mind at all.

140
00:10:49,580 --> 00:10:51,777
I'm afraid I'm not much good as a tank.

141
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:52,690
And anyway,

142
00:10:52,920 --> 00:10:57,214
I'm curious to see whether June and
Tetchy can survive a proper beatdown.

143
00:10:58,060 --> 00:10:59,277
Don't worry about us.

144
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:00,460
We can handle it.

145
00:11:00,820 --> 00:11:01,960
I guess we'll try.

146
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:03,480
Oh, this is good.

147
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:09,580
All right, ready to go take a
peek at that boss room? Yeah!

148
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:16,550
Yeah!

149
00:11:20,760 --> 00:11:21,590
Yeah!

150
00:11:24,020 --> 00:11:25,120
What a team.

151
00:11:25,420 --> 00:11:27,891
I wonder if they really need me after all.

152
00:11:30,140 --> 00:11:33,717
I can't believe how quickly you
guys are clearing the labyrinth.

153
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:35,859
You're an amazing group of players.

154
00:11:39,580 --> 00:11:40,657
It's the boss room!

155
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:41,570
Come on!

156
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:45,380
Yuki, hold it!

157
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:15,950
Look!

158
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:20,240
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

159
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:21,377
Hey, hang on, hang on!

160
00:12:21,460 --> 00:12:22,457
We're not here to fight you!

161
00:12:22,540 --> 00:12:24,117
Then lower your weapons, now!

162
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:25,030
Get rid of it!

163
00:12:25,940 --> 00:12:28,957
Keep your eye on them, and if they
make a move for their weapons,

164
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:31,640
hit them with an Aquabine
spell. You got it.

165
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:35,440
This is our first ever PvP in Halo.

166
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:37,153
It's kind of thrilling.

167
00:12:39,060 --> 00:12:42,236
If you're not PKers, then
why were you hiding from us?

168
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:44,297
We were waiting for someone.

169
00:12:44,380 --> 00:12:45,957
We were hiding because we didn't want to

170
00:12:46,040 --> 00:12:47,897
get hit by a mob before
our friends got here.

171
00:12:47,980 --> 00:12:49,098
You know how it is.

172
00:12:50,700 --> 00:12:51,641
All right, then.

173
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:55,637
We're here to take on the boss, so
if you're not ready to enter yet?

174
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:57,677
We'd like to take a crack at it first!

175
00:12:57,760 --> 00:13:00,060
No, that's cool.

176
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:08,917
We'll just hang here, you
know, till our buddies show up.

177
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,177
Oh and uh, watch your backs in there!

178
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:12,980
Good luck.

179
00:13:17,680 --> 00:13:19,497
Don't give those dudes a second thought!

180
00:13:19,580 --> 00:13:20,717
Come on, let's do this!

181
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:25,360
Don't worry, let's Let's just stick to
the plan and have a look inside, okay?

182
00:13:25,880 --> 00:13:26,710
Okay.

183
00:13:27,620 --> 00:13:31,577
Instead of just scoping it out, let's
bust in there and trash the boss.

184
00:13:31,660 --> 00:13:33,425
If you want to try, go for it.

185
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:38,357
Just make sure not to use any of your
expensive potions and stuff to recover.

186
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:41,277
Siune and I will support you with
healing spells, so fight hard,

187
00:13:41,360 --> 00:13:43,595
but try not to get too far in the red.

188
00:13:43,820 --> 00:13:44,880
Right on, coach!

189
00:13:46,620 --> 00:13:47,450
Listen up.

190
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:49,677
If you die, don't respawn right away.

191
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:52,097
Just hang out and study
the boss's attack patterns.

192
00:13:52,180 --> 00:13:56,697
Then let's meet back at the Lombard save
point and talk about what we learned, okay?

193
00:13:56,780 --> 00:13:57,680
Roger that!

194
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:47,940
Let's get him! Right!

195
00:14:53,680 --> 00:14:54,510
Jeez!

196
00:14:54,640 --> 00:14:55,997
We got our butts kicked!

197
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:57,617
What kind of attack was that?

198
00:14:57,700 --> 00:14:59,700
That's gotta be against the rules!

199
00:14:59,800 --> 00:15:02,271
That boss sure knows how to defend itself.

200
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:03,657
Do you think that's a random move?

201
00:15:03,740 --> 00:15:05,152
Using his arms to block?

202
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:08,140
And we fought so hard, too!

203
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:10,660
Hey! What's wrong?

204
00:15:11,100 --> 00:15:12,276
Come here, you guys.

205
00:15:12,460 --> 00:15:13,290
Gather round.

206
00:15:14,220 --> 00:15:15,050
Huh?

207
00:15:15,133 --> 00:15:17,132
I know you're tired, but we need to talk.

208
00:15:18,580 --> 00:15:21,137
Remember those three guys
standing by the boss room?

209
00:15:21,220 --> 00:15:22,380
Sure. Why?

210
00:15:22,680 --> 00:15:25,997
They were scouts from a guild
that specializes in boss raids.

211
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:26,910
What?

212
00:15:27,100 --> 00:15:31,865
If another guild tries to hit that boss
room, their job is to sit back and watch.

213
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:35,977
The bosses you tried to raid on the
previous floor and the one before that?

214
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:38,197
I have a feeling they were there, too.

215
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:40,360
I had no idea they were even there.

216
00:15:40,860 --> 00:15:44,717
They didn't get in our way or try to
stop us, so they're definitely spies.

217
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:45,997
All they want is intel.

218
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:50,017
And when a small guild like the Sleeping
Knights comes along to take on a boss,

219
00:15:50,100 --> 00:15:54,159
We're helping them figure out all
its attack patterns and weaknesses.

220
00:15:54,860 --> 00:15:55,690
Wait a sec.

221
00:15:55,900 --> 00:15:59,717
The door shut behind us when we were inside,
and they definitely didn't follow us.

222
00:15:59,800 --> 00:16:02,329
So, if they can't see
us fighting the boss,

223
00:16:02,480 --> 00:16:05,127
how are they going to
gather any intel on it?

224
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:07,320
Actually, they could see us fight.

225
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:11,737
Towards the end there, I looked over and
I saw a tiny gray lizard near June's feet.

226
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:14,879
That's when I realized I
let my guard down too soon.

227
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:16,797
It's a dark spell called peeping.

228
00:16:16,880 --> 00:16:20,820
It binds a familiar to a player
and the caster sees what it sees.

229
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:24,840
So what you're saying is,

230
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:29,400
after we got hammered by the
bosses on floors 25 and 6,

231
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:33,937
that other guild swooping in and
beating them, that wasn't a coincidence?

232
00:16:34,020 --> 00:16:35,491
No, I'm afraid it wasn't.

233
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:38,057
You probably fought so
hard the boss used every

234
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:40,517
move it had against you
and they saw it all.

235
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:43,129
That's how they beat
the bosses so quickly.

236
00:16:44,320 --> 00:16:45,737
They used us again.

237
00:16:45,820 --> 00:16:48,740
Now they know everything
about this boss, too.

238
00:16:49,260 --> 00:16:51,672
They're probably in there taking it down.

239
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:56,400
Those dicks. Damn it. Easy, guys.

240
00:16:57,620 --> 00:16:59,300
Don't count us out just yet.

241
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:02,760
But what can we do about it now? Simple.

242
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:05,200
It's 2.30 p .m. in the real world.

243
00:17:05,540 --> 00:17:08,077
At this time of day and
on such short notice,

244
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:11,037
it'll be hard to find enough
people for a raid party.

245
00:17:11,120 --> 00:17:14,417
By my estimate, it should
take them at least an hour.

246
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:16,580
That's plenty of time for us.

247
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:18,240
So here's the deal.

248
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:22,437
After this, if we can get back to that
room in 30 minutes, we can take it.

249
00:17:22,520 --> 00:17:23,350
Okay?

250
00:17:27,840 --> 00:17:28,670
Yeah!

251
00:17:33,580 --> 00:17:35,500
Last one there's a rotten egg!

252
00:17:36,620 --> 00:17:38,180
Hey, wait for us!

253
00:17:38,400 --> 00:17:39,320
Slow bump!

254
00:17:45,140 --> 00:17:45,970
Crap.

255
00:17:46,053 --> 00:17:46,900
We're too late.

256
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:51,830
Don't worry.

257
00:17:52,080 --> 00:17:54,197
They won't advance with only 20 players.

258
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:57,697
We should have enough time to give it
one more try before the rest show up.

259
00:17:57,780 --> 00:17:58,610
You think?

260
00:17:59,560 --> 00:18:00,390
Excuse me.

261
00:18:01,180 --> 00:18:03,497
We'd like to try the boss before you do.

262
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:05,120
Could you guys let us by?

263
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:07,420
Sorry, Dollface.

264
00:18:07,700 --> 00:18:09,759
The boss room's off-limits for now.

265
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,440
Wait, off-limits?

266
00:18:11,540 --> 00:18:13,177
What's that supposed to mean?

267
00:18:13,260 --> 00:18:16,717
It means in a couple minutes, the rest
of the guild's gonna roll up here.

268
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:19,097
We're just holding the room till they do.

269
00:18:19,180 --> 00:18:21,117
If you want, you can wait over there.

270
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:23,435
And how long do you expect us to wait?

271
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:26,340
Um, another hour or so?

272
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:29,158
But we don't have that kind of time.

273
00:18:29,340 --> 00:18:31,957
If you were going in right now,
well, that's a different story.

274
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:34,520
But you're not, so let us go in first.

275
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:36,746
Look, I don't make the rules.

276
00:18:36,840 --> 00:18:40,664
I'm just a grunt here, following
orders like everyone else, okay?

277
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:42,700
Hey, you got a complaint?

278
00:18:43,040 --> 00:18:44,917
Go to the guild headquarters
and talk to them.

279
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:46,997
It's over in Ygg City,
so get - Are you kidding?

280
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:47,997
That's far away!

281
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:50,609
It'd take us at least
an hour to get there!

282
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:52,740
Hey, big guy. Hmm?

283
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:55,177
Just trying to figure things out here.

284
00:18:55,260 --> 00:18:58,997
So, no matter how nice we ask,
you're not gonna let us get by you.

285
00:18:59,080 --> 00:19:00,668
Is that what you're saying?

286
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:02,620
Yeah, that's it.

287
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:04,779
That's pretty much what I'm saying.

288
00:19:06,180 --> 00:19:07,537
Okay, if that's what you're saying.

289
00:19:07,620 --> 00:19:08,640
You wanna fight?

290
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:16,680
But Yuki, are you sure?

291
00:19:17,680 --> 00:19:21,092
Asuna, sometimes you gotta
fight to get your point across.

292
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:25,300
You know, like how dead serious
you are about something.

293
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:26,670
Just saying.

294
00:19:27,340 --> 00:19:29,420
Yep, that's pretty much how it is.

295
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:31,420
You guys...

296
00:19:32,420 --> 00:19:34,977
These folks know exactly
what I'm talking about.

297
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:36,457
They look like the serious types.

298
00:19:36,540 --> 00:19:40,952
We could chop away all day, and they'd
defend this room to the last player.

299
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:43,260
Right, pig guy?

300
00:19:44,740 --> 00:19:46,540
We got orders to...

301
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:52,160
Come on, draw your sword.

302
00:20:12,020 --> 00:20:16,140
You little punk, I'm gonna
make you pay for that.

303
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:27,160
Sometimes you gotta fight
to get your point across.

304
00:20:33,280 --> 00:20:34,940
Yeah, she's right.

305
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:02,400
Hey, guys!

306
00:21:06,540 --> 00:21:09,277
I should have dealt with
this when I had the chance.

307
00:21:09,360 --> 00:21:10,400
Sorry, Asuna.

308
00:21:10,920 --> 00:21:13,280
My big mouth got you into this mess.

309
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:15,540
But it was totally worth it!

310
00:21:16,460 --> 00:21:17,380
Know why?

311
00:21:17,560 --> 00:21:21,260
Because just now, I saw the best
smile I've ever seen on you!

312
00:21:22,140 --> 00:21:25,660
In that case, I'll
start pulling my weight.

313
00:21:26,460 --> 00:21:28,580
We might not take down this boss.

314
00:21:29,260 --> 00:21:33,560
But the next one, I
promise, that one's ours!

315
00:21:36,540 --> 00:21:38,893
Some folks just don't know when to quit.

316
00:21:51,300 --> 00:21:52,500
Sorry, guys.

317
00:21:59,660 --> 00:22:00,780
Stand down.

318
00:22:02,140 --> 00:22:03,900
You're not getting past me.

319
00:23:03,100 --> 00:23:04,417
Thank

320
00:23:04,500 --> 00:23:05,817
you

321
00:23:05,900 --> 00:23:12,900
so

322
00:23:19,760 --> 00:23:26,620
much for watching.

323
00:23:26,900 --> 00:23:33,900
I want to see you
